/country><doc-number>7281633</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-8009197-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8009197</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8317250-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8317250</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1085494A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>FUJITSU GENERAL LTD</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KOBAYASHI MASAYUKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NAKAJIMA MASAMICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>FUJITSU GENERAL LIMITED</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KOBAYASHI, MASAYUKI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NAKAJIMA, MASAMICHI</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KOBAYASHI MASAYUKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NAKAJIMA MASAMICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KOBAYASHI, MASAYUKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NAKAJIMA, MASAMICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An image quality correcting circuit includes a mean calculating section (10) for calculating the mean of luminance level of each pixel of the video signal received at the video signal input terminal (12), an occurrence counter (13) for counting the occurrences of each luminance level calculated by the mean calculating section (10) for every predetermined levels, a linear interpolating section (15) for drawing a correction characteristic line by linear interpolation according to the count output point of the occurrence counter (13), and an image quality correcting section (16) for correcting the inputted video signal by using the correction characteristics line.  The correction characteristic line is a line continuously consisting of linearly interpolated lines draw on a diagram showing the luminance level as the abscissas and the occurrence as the ordinates.  The image quality correcting section (16) corrects the video signal inputted through the image signal input terminal (12) by using the correction characteristic line.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un circuit de correction de qualité d'image, qui comprend une unité de calcul de moyenne (10) conçue pour calculer la moyenne du niveau de luminance de chaque pixel du signal vidéo reçu au niveau d'un terminal d'entrée de signal vidéo (12), un compteur d'occurrence (13) conçu pour compter les occurrences de chaque niveau de luminance calculé par l'unité de calcul de moyenne (10) pour chaque niveau prédéterminé, une unité d'interpolation linéaire (15) qui dessine une ligne caractéristique de correction par interpolation linéaire en fonction du point de sortie de comptage du compteur d'occurrences (13), et une unité de correction de qualité d'image (16) qui corrige le signal vidéo entré, au moyen de la ligne caractéristique de correction. La ligne caractéristique de correction est une ligne formée en continu de lignes interpolées de manière linéaire tracées sur un graphique représentant le niveau de luminance dans les abscisses et les occurrences dans les ordonnées. L'unité de correction d'image (16) corrige le signal vidéo entré par le terminal d'entrée de signal d'image (12) en utilisant la ligne caractéristique de correction.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>